<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37605" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-fŏdĭo</span></b> ,
			fōdi, 3, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To dig before</i> or <i>in front
			of</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">portas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 11, 473</span></i>
			 (id est ante portas fossas faciunt, Serv.).
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> With
			respect to time, <i>to dig</i> or <i>bury
				before</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scrobes,</span>”
				<i>to make pits beforehand</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 11, 16, § 79</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurum,</span>”
				<i>to bury before</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					13, 60</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
